<div style="border: 2px solid #1a5276; padding: 15px; text-align: center; background-color: #e0f2f7; margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <h1 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Learning to Relax – Lesson # 4</h1>
    <p style="color: #1a5276; margin: 5px 0 0 0;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 4</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Writing</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Grade:</b> 12th Grade (CEFR: B1.3)</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Scenario:</b> Learning to Balance</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Theme:</b> Learning to Relax</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Writing: Productive: Write reflective essays on personal experiences. Interactive: Write a group text on various topics, collaboratively, to be shared in a digital format.</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Writing: Can write a reflective essay on the experience of balancing school and personal life (e.g., "In my essay, I'll describe how to manage my schoolwork alongside personal activities like sports and volunteering.") Can collaboratively write a digital text about learning to relax or maintaining school-life balance (e.g., "Take breaks during study sessions and make time for hobbies to relax and recharge.") Can exchange drafts and provide feedback to improve the group's digital text (e.g., "Suggest ways to make the blog post more engaging for readers.")</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 30px;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333; background-color: #f0f8ff;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px; color: #1a5276; width: 30%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px; color: #1a5276; width: 50%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px; color: #1a5276; width: 20%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b><br>Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays a series of images (e.g., a student studying late, someone practicing mindfulness, friends socializing, a person jogging). Students are asked to quickly jot down one word or short phrase for each image that describes how it relates to 'balance' or 'relaxation'. Then, they briefly share their word/phrase with a partner.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher projects a short, simple paragraph describing their own efforts to balance work and personal life, e.g., "I <i>have been practicing mindfulness</i> to <i>relieve stress</i>. If I <i>had more time</i>, I <i>would exercise</i> more." The teacher reads the paragraph aloud, modeling the pronunciation of key vocabulary like "activities" (/ækˈtɪvɪtɪz/) and "relieve" (/rɪˈliːv/), emphasizing the vowel sounds. The teacher also highlights the use of the present perfect continuous and second conditional in the text.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What does 'mindfulness' mean? Is it about rushing or focusing on the present?" (Focus on vocabulary: mindfulness, focus, relax)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"When I say, 'If I had more time, I would exercise,' am I talking about a real situation or a hypothetical one?" (Focus on grammar: second conditional)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b><br>Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Learning to Balance"</p></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short reflective essay excerpt or a blog post titled "My Journey to a Balanced Routine" (digital format, projected). The text should be B1.3 level and naturally incorporate the target grammar (Present perfect continuous, Second conditional, Modals for possibility) and vocabulary (e.g., <i>balance, routine, activities, schedule, stress, relaxation, mindfulness, time management, procrastinate, relieve, prioritize</i>).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Comprehending and analyzing written texts that reflect personal experiences and suggest strategies for maintaining school-life balance and relaxation.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist questions:</b> "What is the author's main challenge described in the essay?" and "What is the primary purpose of this text?" (Students write their answers individually).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Identify Strategies:</b> "List three specific strategies the author mentions for managing their <i>workload</i> and finding <i>relaxation</i>." (Students underline or highlight within the text and then write them down).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Grammar Focus:</b> "Find and copy one sentence that uses the Present Perfect Continuous and one that uses a Second Conditional."</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">8-10 min</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b><br>Accuracy focus on Writing</p></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students will practice writing sentences and short paragraphs using the Present Perfect Continuous, Second Conditional, and Modals for possibility, integrating vocabulary related to "balance," "routine," "stress," and "relaxation." They will practice giving suggestions and expressing opinions in writing.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled Practice (Sentence Completion):</b> Students complete sentences using the correct form of the verb (Present Perfect Continuous) or a suitable modal of possibility (<i>should, might, could, may</i>), and a target vocabulary word. For example: "I _______ (try) new <i>hobbies</i> to ____________ (relax) recently." (I <i>have been trying</i> new hobbies to <i>relax</i> recently.) or "You _________ (set goals) to improve your <i>time management</i>." (You <i>might set goals</i> to improve your time management.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-controlled Practice (Sentence Transformation):</b> Students are given simple statements about lack of balance or stress and transform them into sentences using the Second Conditional to express hypothetical improvements, and then add a suggestion using a modal verb. For example: "I don't have enough <i>downtime</i>." → "If I <i>had more downtime</i>, I <i>would spend</i> it on <i>restorative activities</i>. You <i>should also prioritize</i> your <i>wellbeing</i>." They focus on creating complex sentences.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Guided Paragraph Writing (Collaborative & Peer Check):</b> In pairs, students are given prompts such as "Describe an ongoing effort you've been making to manage your <i>workload</i> and reduce <i>procrastination</i>" or "Imagine a perfect <i>routine</i> for a <i>balanced social life</i> and academics. What <i>would you do</i> differently?" Each pair writes a short paragraph (4-5 sentences) incorporating at least one Present Perfect Continuous sentence, one Second Conditional sentence, and two modal verbs for suggestions. Once done, pairs exchange their paragraphs and check for correct grammar, appropriate vocabulary usage, and clarity, making notes for their peers.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">15-18 min</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b><br>Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Learning to Balance"</p></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Collaborative digital text creation (e.g., a shared online document, a simple blog post draft). Students work in groups of 3-4 to collaboratively write a section of a class "Online Guide to Balancing School and Life in Panama." Each group focuses on a specific sub-topic related to the theme "Learning to Relax" and the scenario "Learning to Balance."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Groups are assigned different topics such as "Effective <i>Time Management</i>," "The Power of <i>Mindfulness</i>," "The Role of <i>Hobbies</i> and <i>Social Life</i>," or "Setting Healthy <i>Boundaries</i>."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Each group writes a paragraph (approx. 80-100 words) for their section. They must include:
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">At least one sentence using the Present Perfect Continuous to describe ongoing efforts (e.g., "We <i>have been exploring</i> different <i>time management</i> apps...").</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">At least one sentence using the Second Conditional to discuss hypothetical improvements (e.g., "If students <i>prioritized</i> their <i>downtime</i>, they <i>would feel</i> less <i>overwhelmed</i>.").</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">At least two suggestions using modals for possibility (<i>should, might, can, could, may</i>) (e.g., "You <i>might</i> try the Pomodoro technique," "Students <i>should set aside</i> specific times for <i>relaxation</i>.").</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">A minimum of five vocabulary words from the list (<i>balance, stress, relaxation, wellbeing, activities, schedule, flexibility, organize, reflect</i>).</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Groups are encouraged to share their cultural perspectives on managing stress and achieving balance, fostering inclusive communication as they write (Sociolinguistic Competence).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher monitors groups, provides assistance with vocabulary and grammar, and ensures collaborative participation.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10-12 min</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b><br>Formative assessment strategy</p></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Peer feedback and teacher observation using a simple rubric.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Each group exchanges their collaboratively written digital text section with another group. Using a peer feedback form, students provide written feedback and suggestions for improvement on the other group's text. They focus on clarity, content related to the topic, correct usage of target grammar, and appropriate vocabulary. (e.g., "Your explanation of '<i>mindfulness</i>' is clear, but you <i>might add</i> another suggestion using a modal verb."). Teacher observes group interactions and written feedback quality, noting instances of giving suggestions and expressing opinions.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (rubric points):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity and relevance of content to the sub-topic.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Correct and appropriate use of Present Perfect Continuous (Grammar).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Correct and appropriate use of Second Conditional (Grammar).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Correct and appropriate use of Modals for possibility (Grammar/Pragmatic - Giving Suggestions).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Effective integration of target vocabulary (<i>balance, stress, relaxation, mindfulness, routine, activities, workload, etc.</i>).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Collaborative contribution from all group members (Sociolinguistic).</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students answer the following prompts individually:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was the most challenging part of writing your group's section, and how did you overcome it?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"List one new strategy for maintaining school-life balance or relaxing that you learned from your group or another group's text."</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">8-10 min</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How has working collaboratively on this digital text helped you to better express ideas about 'Learning to Relax' and 'Learning to Balance' in writing?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What grammatical structures (e.g., Present Perfect Continuous, Second Conditional) or vocabulary did you find most useful for conveying your personal experiences or suggestions, and why?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What aspects of the writing activities worked well for 12th graders? Did they successfully incorporate the target grammar (Present Perfect Continuous, Second Conditional, Modals for possibility) and vocabulary into their collaborative texts?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or additional scaffolds are needed for students who struggled with forming complex sentences or providing constructive feedback in writing? (e.g., provide sentence starters for feedback, review specific grammar points).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">How did the collaborative nature of the task encourage inclusive communication and sharing of cultural perspectives on stress management?</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson in the theme sequence:</b> The collaboratively written digital text sections will be used in Lesson 5 (Mediation & Integration). Students will summarize, consolidate, and present the information from their group's section to the class, possibly explaining or mediating the content for a wider audience, and then integrate it into a larger 21st-Century Skills project on promoting wellbeing.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">4-5 min</p></td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>